  => STEP 2 PASS: in the 6.2.40 U-Boot shell `date reset` resets the RTC to 2000-01-01
     and `date` sets it to each of a past, current and future date, each read back
     exactly as written. After a U-Boot `reset` and a full boot, AW+ `show clock` reads
     5 Nov 2026 01:03:49, the date U-Boot last wrote plus the boot time. That date
     could only come from U-Boot, so AW+ took its time from the RTC that U-Boot set.
     The config is unchanged after tear_down and the exception log is empty.

